Vault
A small and lightweight program and game launcher via CLI, written in Bash!
===========================================================================


What is Vault?
--------------

Vault started as an individual and private project with a single purpose: to solve my problem of bringing together various Linux/Wine games in a centralized, secure, and above all, clean and organized location.
However, after achieving the first minimally stable version (which is not the case with the current one), I simply uploaded the project publicly.
It's just a hobby and a way to automate tedious and repetitive tasks.


Installation:
-------------

	$ curl -Os https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sakaki91/vault/refs/heads/main/vault && bash vault

If you don't have your local binaries folder set up, please run:

	$ echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' >> "$HOME"/.bashrc

or if you use zsh/fish, adapt it to your shell's .rc file.


* But why??

This allows you to call it using only "vault" in the terminal, but using your local binaries folder, without interfering with the system's root directories.
